# The room keeper restarted in QEMU (TASK-26 Q7; ADR-0269, proposed ADR-0293
# and ADR-0298; gate rows keeper-restart, keeper-reconnect and prompt-rebind
# of tools/untrusted-gate.txt). On the test image (feature net-test), `room
# crash-keeper` asks init to end the keeper with the room running:
#  - keeper-restart: init starts a new keeper, which finds the room's job again
#    with its limits and its process (INV-0269-1 to INV-0269-3): the limit still
#    refuses, `top` still counts the process, the room has one job;
#  - keeper-reconnect: the shell's next request (`room set`) goes over a new
#    channel that init gives on the reconnect channel, and the keeper applies it
#    to the same job;
#  - prompt-rebind: the prompt before the next line rebinds the shell to the
#    keeper (zosh calls the keeper's pump before each prompt), so the prompt
#    keeps the room's name and its lines keep running in the room's job. The
#    test image's init prints a line when it answers a reconnect; it must come
#    right after the restart, before any keeper call (a call rebinds lazily).
#  - `sleep 300` in the room survives the restart (`top` counts it: 1 of 16)
#    and `room remove --kill` ends it (INV-0269-3).
! panicked
! storage failed
< Type help to begin
< \r\n~> 
> room new agent-1 --mem 64M --procs 16 +w /t/w\r
< agent-1 --colour 1 --mem 64M --procs 16 +w /t/w
< \r\n~> 
> room agent-1\r
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> sleep 300 &\r
< [1] sleep 300
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> top\r
< agent-1
< of 64M
< 1 of 16
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# keeper-restart: the keeper ends; init starts another.
> room crash-keeper\r
< init: the shell asked the room keeper to end
< init: the room keeper ended
< init: the room keeper was restarted
# prompt-rebind: the prompt before the next line rebinds the shell, before any
# keeper call: `init` says it answered a reconnect right after the restart, and
# the prompt follows. (The first keeper call would otherwise rebind lazily and
# hide a prompt that does not.)
< init: the shell reconnected to the room keeper
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# The prompt still names the room, and the line runs in its job.
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 64M --procs 16  (room agent-1)
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> top\r
< agent-1
< of 64M
< 1 of 16
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# The kept job still refuses at its limit (INV-0266-1, INV-0269-1).
> memhog\r
< memhog: refused after
< hint: room agent-1 is at its memory limit of 64M
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# keeper-reconnect: a request over the new channel reaches the same job.
> room set agent-1 --mem 48M\r
< agent-1 --colour 1 --mem 48M --procs 16 +w /t/w
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 48M --procs 16  (room agent-1)
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# A second end of the keeper and the same again.
> room crash-keeper\r
< init: the room keeper was restarted
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> memhog\r
< memhog: refused after
< hint: room agent-1 is at its memory limit of 48M
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> room --leave\r
# The prompt outside the room starts its line; "agent-1 /t/w> " would also
# hold "/t/w> " (TASK-29, V14).
< \r\n/t/w> 
> room remove agent-1 --kill\r
< /t/w> 
> room\r
< home
< sleep 300: killed
< /t/w> 
> poweroff\r
